---
import pkg from '../../../package.json';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>pokéharness</title>
<meta name="description" content="pokéharness turns every claude, codex, or cursor session running on your machine into a walker in a pixel-art garden — spawn one, watch it work, and see what it's doing without staring at a terminal.">
<meta property="og:title" content="pokéharness">
<meta property="og:description" content="pokéharness turns every claude, codex, or cursor session running on your machine into a walker in a pixel-art garden.">
<meta property="og:image" content="https://pokeharness.parthkohale.com/og.png">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png">

<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Press Start 2P';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('/fonts/press-start-2p-latin-400.woff2') format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 700;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('/fonts/inter-latin-var.woff2') format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 700;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('/fonts/jetbrains-mono-latin-var.woff2') format('woff2');
  }

  :root {
    --ground-0: #17171B;
    --ground-100: #1D1D22;
    --ground-200: #26262C;
    --border: #787684;
    --ink-900: #DEDBD6;
    --ink-700: #B3B0AC;
    --ink-500: #96919F;
    --gold: #E8B740;
    --on-accent: #1A1320;
    --coral: #E08C82;
    --mint: #74C096;
    --sky: #6FB3C4;
    --lemon: #CFAA57;
    --lilac: #A896E3;
    --peach: #DFA57F;
    --font-display: 'Press Start 2P', monospace;
    --font-ui: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;
    --font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  html { color-scheme: dark; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--ground-0);
    color: var(--ink-900);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  a { color: var(--gold); }

  img { display: block; max-width: 100%; }

  :focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--gold);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .wrap {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  /* ── top wordmark ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .brand-row {
    padding: 24px 0 0;
  }
  .brand {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  /* ── hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    padding: 32px 0 48px;
  }
  .hero-text {
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 56px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .hero p.subhead {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    max-width: 560px;
  }
  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 12px 22px;
    border-radius: 0;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--gold);
    color: var(--on-accent);
  }
  .btn-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.4);
  }
  .hero-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
  }

  /* ── demo frame ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .demo-shell {
    padding: 8px 0 8px;
  }
  .window-chrome {
    background: var(--ground-200);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    padding: 8px 10px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 7px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .dot {
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .dot-red { background: #FF5F57; }
  .dot-yellow { background: #FEBC2E; }
  .dot-green { background: #28C840; }
  .demo-frame-body {
    background: var(--ground-100);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    border-top: none;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
  }
  /* The demo has its own internal breakpoints tuned for a real desktop app
     window and breaks down below ~800px of *iframe* width. Rather than let
     the iframe shrink (which would trigger those internal breakpoints and
     clip content), we render it at a fixed design width and scale the whole
     box down visually with a transform — the iframe always sees ~1040px of
     internal viewport, and the visitor sees it fit whatever space is
     available. 1040/650 keeps the same 16:10 ratio as the frame itself, so
     the scale factor is just container-width / 1040. */
  .demo-frame-scaler {
    width: 1040px;
    height: 650px;
    transform-origin: top left;
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
  }
  .demo-frame-scaler iframe {
    width: 1040px;
    height: 650px;
    border: 0;
    display: block;
  }
  .demo-caption {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .demo-mobile-note {
    display: none;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .demo-mobile-note { display: block; }
  }

  /* ── works with ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .works-with {
    padding: 48px 0 8px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    background: var(--ground-200);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.25);
    padding: 4px 8px;
  }

  /* ── how it works ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .section {
    padding: 56px 0;
  }
  .section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 22px;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .step-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .step h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .step p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .step img {
    width: 100%;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
  }

  /* ── feature grid ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .features {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .feature-card {
    background: var(--ground-100);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    border-left-width: 3px;
    border-left-style: solid;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .feature-media {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    background: var(--ground-200);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .feature-media img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .feature-media.solid {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .feature-body {
    padding: 16px 18px 20px;
  }
  .feature-body h3 {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .feature-body p {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── footer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    padding: 32px 0 48px;
  }
  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .disclaimer {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  /* ── responsive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .features { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .features { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 30px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="wrap brand-row">
  <div class="brand">pokéharness</div>
</div>

<header class="hero wrap">
  <div class="hero-text">
    <h1>your coding agents, as pokémon in a garden</h1>
    <p class="subhead">pokéharness turns every claude, codex, or cursor session running on your machine into a walker in a pixel-art garden — spawn one, watch it work, and see what it's doing without staring at a terminal.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/mavericksxx/pokemon-harness/releases/latest">download for mac</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/mavericksxx/pokemon-harness">browse the source</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-tag">v{pkg.version} · free, local, no accounts, no cloud</div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap demo-shell">
  <div class="window-chrome">
    <span class="dot dot-red"></span>
    <span class="dot dot-yellow"></span>
    <span class="dot dot-green"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="demo-frame-body" id="demo-frame-body">
    <div class="demo-frame-scaler" id="demo-frame-scaler">
      <iframe src="/demo.html" title="pokéharness live demo" loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="demo-caption">click spawn, shiny, or battle inside it — every animation is the same engine running in the real app. nothing here is a recording.</p>
  <p class="demo-mobile-note">best explored with a mouse — the demo above is scaled down to fit, so hover effects and small buttons are easiest on a bigger screen.</p>
</div>
<script>
  (function () {
    var DESIGN_WIDTH = 1040;
    var body = document.getElementById('demo-frame-body');
    var scaler = document.getElementById('demo-frame-scaler');
    if (!body || !scaler) return;
    function fit() {
      var scale = body.clientWidth / DESIGN_WIDTH;
      scaler.style.transform = 'scale(' + scale + ')';
    }
    fit();
    window.addEventListener('resize', fit);
  })();
</script>

<div class="wrap works-with">
  <span>works with the coding-agent cli you already have</span>
  <span class="tag">claude</span>
  <span class="tag">codex</span>
  <span class="tag">cursor-agent</span>
</div>

<section class="section wrap">
  <h2>how it works</h2>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">1</div>
      <h3>download and open it</h3>
      <p>one .zip, drag it to applications. gatekeeper will ask once — right-click, open, open. that's the whole install.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">2</div>
      <h3>spawn a session</h3>
      <p>point it at a project folder and pick a pokémon, or let it pick a random starter. it launches claude, codex, or cursor-agent right there, the same as running it in a terminal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">3</div>
      <h3>watch it work</h3>
      <p>tool calls show as a speech bubble and a walk to the right spot in the garden. subagents spawn as battles. long sessions evolve. everything you'd see scrolling past in the terminal, you now see from across the room.</p>
      <img src="/screenshots/garden.png" alt="a few walkers roaming the garden, mid tool-call, with speech bubbles above them">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
  <h2>what's in the garden</h2>
  <div class="features">
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--coral)">
      <div class="feature-media solid" style="background: rgba(224, 140, 130, 0.12)">
        <img src="/screenshots/garden.png" alt="the pixel-art garden" style="opacity: 0.85">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>shiny pokémon</h3>
        <p>every session rolls shiny once, 1-in-64, kept for life. a sparkle burst and a star badge — no different from the games.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--mint)">
      <div class="feature-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/evolution.png" alt="an evolution ceremony mid-flash, the walker's old form as a white silhouette">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>evolution</h3>
        <p>working time adds up. cross a threshold and the walker plays a real evolution ceremony — flash, silhouette, the old/new-form blur — then comes out the other side stronger, sometimes flies.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--sky)">
      <div class="feature-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/battle.png" alt="two walkers squared up mid-battle, move text overhead">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>subagent battles</h3>
        <p>a task tool call spawns a wild pokémon and a real battle: lunges, hit flashes, move text, up to three at once.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--lemon)">
      <div class="feature-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/mega.png" alt="a mega-evolved charizard mid-battle, gold ring and sparkle burst around it, a floating 'mega evolved!' text overhead">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>mega evolution</h3>
        <p>a handful of species mega-evolve mid-battle with a full ring, vortex, and plume ceremony, then revert when the fight ends.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--lilac)">
      <div class="feature-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/arceus.png" alt="the garden replaced by a starfield cosmos, arceus floating and cycling through its type-plate formes">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>arceus</h3>
        <p>summon a real claude session as arceus — a permanent, gold-framed orchestrator that can hand work to any other session in the garden.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--peach)">
      <div class="feature-media solid" style="background: rgba(223, 165, 127, 0.12)">
        <img src="/screenshots/garden.png" alt="the pixel-art garden" style="opacity: 0.85">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>day and night</h3>
        <p>the garden tracks your actual local clock. lamps flicker on at dusk, the pond catches moonlight, and it fades back at sunrise.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer class="wrap">
  <div class="footer-links">
    <a href="https://github.com/mavericksxx/pokemon-harness">github repo</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/mavericksxx/pokemon-harness/releases/latest">download for mac</a>
    <a href="/docs/">docs</a>
  </div>
  <p class="disclaimer">Pokémon, Pokémon character names, and their designs are trademarks of Nintendo, Game Freak, and Creatures Inc. Sprites shown here are fan-made and used non-commercially; this project is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of them.</p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
